se":"R404.1.5.2","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.wall.thickness.masonry","value":">= thickness of wall supported; 8 in nominal allowed under brick-veneered frame and 10 in cavity walls if supported height <= 20 ft","clause":"R404.1.5.1","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.wall.height_above_grade","value":">= 4 in with masonry veneer; >= 6 in elsewhere","clause":"R404.1.6","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.crawl.vent.area","value":"1 sq ft net per 150 sq ft under-floor area","clause":"R408.2","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.crawl.vent.area.vapor","value":"1/1500 of under-floor area with Class I vapor retarder on ground","clause":"R408.2 Exception 1","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.crawl.vent.corner","value":"one opening within 3 ft of each external corner","clause":"R408.2","note":"Exception 2: not required with Class I vapor retarder if cross ventilation provided","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.crawl.vent.screen","value":"covering least dimension <= 1/4 in","clause":"R408.2","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.crawl.unvented","value":"continuous Class I vapor retarder, laps 6 in sealed, up stem wall 6 in; plus exhaust or conditioned air 1 cfm per 50 sq ft, or plenum, or dehumidification","clause":"R408.3","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.crawl.access.floor","value":">= 18 in x 24 in","clause":"R408.4","note":"through floor","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.crawl.access.wall","value":">= 16 in x 24 in","clause":"R408.4","note":"through perimeter wall; areaway >= 16 x 24 in where below grade; not under a door","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.slab.thickness.min","value":"3.5 in","clause":"R506.1","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.slab.fill.max","value":"24 in clean sand/gravel; 8 in earth (unless approved)","clause":"R506.3.1","note":"","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.slab.base","value":"4 in base course where slab is below grade; not required on Group I soils","clause":"R506.3.2","note":"Table R401.4.1(2)","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.slab.vapor_retarder","value":"6 mil polyethylene or approved, laps >= 6 in","clause":"R506.3.3","note":"not required: unheated garages/accessory, unheated storage < 70 sq ft, carports, flatwork, or building-official approval","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.footing.sdc_d.continuous","value":"continuous footings per Table R403.1.2 (exterior walls always; interior braced wall panels by stories, plan dimension 50 ft, SDC)","clause":"R403.1.2","note":"new table in 2024","confirmed":true},{"id":"found.slab.post_tensioned","value":"post-tensioned slabs per PTI DC10.5","clause":"R506.2","note":"new in 2024","confirmed":true}],"soil_table":{"id":"Table R401.4.1(1)","rows":[{"class":"Crystalline bedrock","psf":12000},{"class":"Sedimentary and foliated rock","psf":4000},{"class":"Sandy gravel and/or gravel (GW, GP)","psf":3000},{"class":"Sand, silty sand, clayey sand, silty gravel, clayey gravel (SW, SP, SM, SC, GM, GC)","psf":2000},{"class":"Clay, sandy clay, silty clay, clayey silt, silt, sandy silt clay (CL, ML, MH, CH)","psf":1500,"note":"footnote b: soils likely < 1500 psf -> soils investigation"}]}}},"notes":"Footing tables in 2021 and 2024 are NOT stories x construction rows: they are three tables by construction (R403.1(1) light frame, (2) brick veneer or lath and plaster, (3) cast-in-place concrete or partially grouted masonry), each with rows load (20 roof live/25 snow, 30, 50, 70 psf) x stories 1-3 x slab/crawl/basement. There is no '8 in solid or fully grouted masonry' table in these editions. All 108 rows are identical in 2021 and 2024. Source typo in both editions: Table R403.1(2), 50 psf, 1 story plus basement, 1500 psf prints '20 x 60' (thickness 60 is obviously wrong; neighbours suggest 6 to 7) - kept verbatim, treat as not confirmed. 2024 renumbering: Table R401.4.1 -> R401.4.1(1) and new R401.4.1(2) soil classes (replaces Table R405.1 references); Tables R404.1.1(1)-(4) -> R404.1.2.1(1)-(4); R404.1.2(1)-(9) -> R404.1.3.2(1)-(9); new Table R403.1.2 (SDC D continuous footings); R506.2.x -> R506.3.x (new R506.2 post-tensioned slabs); vapor retarder R506.2.3 -> R506.3.3. Slab vapor retarder differs: the 2021 viewer text reads 10 mil ASTM E1745 Class A; 2024 reads 6 mil polyethylene or approved. Slope setbacks (H/2 <= 15 ft, H/3 <= 40 ft) are read from Figure R403.1.7.1 image (same in both). No single 7.5 in concrete wall thickness rule exists in ch.4; thickness comes from R404.1.5.2 (>= wall above), Table R608.3 cross-sections, and the 6/8/10 in nominal reinforcement tables. Frost depth is a local value in Table R301.2. Unchanged between editions: R403.1.1, R403.1.4, R403.1.4.1, R403.1.6, R403.1.6.1, R403.1.7.x, R404.1.1, R404.1.6, R408.2-R408.4, R506.1."}
